.TH XNLINKFINDER 1 "January 2026" "xnLinkFinder-Z 7.18" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
xnLinkFinder \- Advanced endpoint discovery and security testing tool
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B xnLinkFinder
[\fIOPTION\fR]... \fI-i INPUT\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
xnLinkFinder-Z is an advanced tool for discovering endpoints, analyzing APIs, and performing security testing.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-input =\fIURL/FILE\fR
Input URL, file of URLs, directory, or Burp/ZAP/Caido file
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-output =\fIFILE\fR
Output file for discovered links (default: output.txt)
.TP
.BR \-\-scan\-cors
Scan for CORS misconfigurations
.TP
.BR \-\-scan\-jwt
Analyze JWT tokens
.TP
.BR \-\-server
Start REST API server mode
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Basic scan:
.B xnLinkFinder -i https://example.com -o results.txt
.TP
Security scanning:
.B xnLinkFinder -i urls.txt --scan-cors --scan-jwt
.TP
Server mode:
.B xnLinkFinder --server --server-port 8080
.SH SEE ALSO
Full documentation at: https://github.com/ZeidMahmoud/xnLinkFinder-Z
.SH AUTHOR
@xnl-h4ck3r, Enhanced by ZeidMahmoud
